  <text>
      <body>
         <p>NEW YEAR'S PARTY 1979
            …New Year’s Eve in Seattle saw one of the most
            all around amusing parties in years--local
            freaks packed the enemy’s practice studio
            to down Guyana punch + dance their hearts
            away to the way out sounds of the Radio’s,
            The St. Bernard Quartet, The Girls, The Enemy,
            The Fishsticks, The Mystery Horns, not to
            mention an outstanding display of charisma by
            George “Johnny Ray” Gleason + The Boppin’ Sounds
            of Rick “Buddy Holly” Smith…Lots more bands but
            we can't remember ‘em all (Cheaters? Electric Tramps?)
            ...Tons of fun…stupid hats, champagne, noisemakers
            + Everything! Wow! (A nite to remember 
            fo’ sho’!!)
            
            ! -> Photos L to R from top:
            
            Rick Smith
            + Nina
            
            Mystery Horns 
            Homer, Roland, + 
            Edward Cardboard
            
            Mass
            Hysteria
            
            Fishsticks
            (World Premiere!)
            
            Tammy
            Smith
            
            The
            Enemy
            (Suzy + George)
            
            Gregor Gayden
            (St. Bernard Qt.)
            
            George… “If your 
            Heartaches..!”
            
            Bob Kondraic 
            w/Cambea
            
            More Hysteria
            (Yahoo! 
            Yreka!)
            
            Damon (?)
            Titus
            
            Don Harper,
            Er. So on–
            –Deeyow!!
            
            (Sorry if we forgot ya!)
            
            Photos: Randy Hall
         </p>
